+## Example spotlight: deploy-watch
+
+[`deploy-watch.yaml`](deploy-watch.yaml) proves the `poll-until` pattern: an external deploy
+status endpoint owns the loop's stop condition, while the agent only intervenes when the status is
+red. Use it when progress is decided by a remote system you can poll, such as a deploy, job, or
+service health check, and you want bounded retries plus a clear breakpoint instead of an
+open-ended "keep checking" script.
